[about]
Title=03 - Key Patterns
Intro=The rules every key follows, so a key can be guessed before it is learned.
Setup=_APP_ is installed and your reader is running.
Homework=Guess three keys before you look them up, then check with Control plus F1.

[step]

Say=A key is named for a word of its command, never from the middle of a word.
Key=
Hear=

[step]

Say=Control does; Shift asks and changes nothing; adding Shift reverses.
Key=
Hear=

[step]

Say=Alt plus Shift plus a letter is a command with no control of its own.
Key=
Hear=

[step]

Say=The function keys follow Windows: F1 help, F2 edit, F3 find again, F4 pick, F5 refresh, F10 menus, F11 version, F12 files.
Key=
Hear=

[step]

Say=What this walk taught: the keys you heard.
